+/*
+ * Data protection on a volume without content protection (a UniXNU owner Data volume is an unencrypted APFS volume, MNT_CPROTECT
+ * clear). APFS answers class 0 ("none") for every file there and keeps no class a caller sets, so a daemon that sets one and checks
+ * it back never sees it: PosterBoard creates its poster data store with NSFileProtectionNone (class D), finds the class missing,
+ * judges the store not viable and has no wallpaper. With boot-arg owner-dataprotect=1 a writable volume without content
+ * protection keeps the class a caller sets in an extended attribute, and a file without one reads as class D, which is what an
+ * unencrypted file is. Nothing is encrypted either way.
